@Jeremy Swinarton's suggestion was to have "Copy 1 link in group" string in situations in which a tab group has multiple tabs, but only one is eligible to be copied (the rest are about:blank, about:preferences, etc). 
Let's go forward with it, as it could be genuinely confusing to see "Copy link" string (and wonder why others are not counted) in a corner case like this. 
cc @DJ Walker @Amy Lee

Organize your tabs with tab groups
Drag one tab onto another to create a group and stay focused when browsing.
@Amy Lee

@Laura Lopez @Ania Safko – Hi, I wanted to propose a toast notification here for users that hit "save and close group" the first 3 times they close a tab group. This follows the same pattern as bookmarks where the first 3 times a bookmark is saved a toast notification appears.

Rational: We've heard in several cases and also with internal employees that they don't know where their group is saved – They might have missed the initial onboarding pop-up.

I spoke to engineering and this is an easy implementation since we already have toast notifications that we can repurpose.

@Amy Lee IA-wise, I think this should move up to better align with the more destructive actions. I'll ask eng if it's easy to do that. 

If it is, I'll suggest we move it. 
If it's hard to do, we can keep it at the bottom for now.

@Amy Lee  could you check in with accessibility and see what the appropriate way to handle adding a "disabled" state to these swatches. I have a quick fix on them now with 50% opacity but seems like there is a slight concern. 

"So I think changing the opacity is probably fine in prefers-contrast, but in forced-colors mode we would still want to use GrayText as the background color to convey that an item is disabled." from Hanna Jones. 

She mentioned to see what accessibility said about the design.

@Laura Lopez -  These bits are reading duplicate.

Rough riff:
Firefox can use AI to suggest tabs and group names. It does it by reading the titles of tabs you have open.

Please add a note that the tab count should be communicated as a description for this item. 
@Anna Yeddi I think it might be helpful to communicate the open/closed status for each of the individual groups, appending each label with "open" or "closed". Does that sound reasonable or is that too verbose? 
Also, what do you think about grouping these items (open groups, closed groups) in two unordered lists to allow for quick navigation?

@Amy Lee Re @Anu Mohajerjasbi 's comment in the Usability Testing Notes doc: there are two different UIs in this list of all tab groups. The groups beneath the Saved Groups heading have a sub-menu to view members. Groups below the horizontal rule display their members via an accordion UI. Do we need two?

Second question: If Saved Groups are above the horizontal rule, are the unsaved below? I suspect the distinction is not about whether the group is saved, but whether it is visible on a tab bar. Groups above the rule are not on a tab bar, groups below the rule are on a tab bar (whether Save Group is on or off). How do we communicate that distinction, plus the save status?

@Laura Lopez When we close a saved group, what should we call it?

@Dave Townsend Hey Mossop! Tech Q: if someone hides a group, they're not explicitly closing it. 

From a tech perspective, is it possible for a user who wants to hide a group, have it NOT show up under Recently closed tabs? 

cc @Amy Lee @Stefan Smagula

